Head of Data Science 

  About our Client: We are currently working with an ASX Top 20 ASX listed organisation who are undertaking a large Data led transformation. A new Head of Data Science is needed to build and drive DS capability within the
    organisation.
  Data is a key to driving innovation within this organisation, at is core Data Science is a key tool needed to drive their commercial success over the next 24 months.
  The Role:
   An inspirational business leader with a unique blend of hands on and managerial experience in the delivery of leading data science solutions and products. The role has three key deliverables:
  1 - Build and develop a market leading team of data scientists;
  2 - Manage c-level stakeholders and influence to drive a data agenda;
  3 - Build data solutions and products allowing the business to drive commercial success.

  You will be a passionate Data scientist with a hunger to take on a career defining opportunity. This is a once in a lifetime role to own and drive Data science capability within an enterprise level organisation.
  You will be the master of your own destiny within this organisation. My client is looking for future business leaders and will invest heavily to develop you and you team into a market leading data science practice within the APAC region.Experience:
  Create business case for Data science strategy, presenting to c-level to secure buy in;
    Implement and deliver data strategy across the organisation aligned with core business goals for 2019 and beyond;
    Create manage the end to end project road map;
    Develop a core team of market leading Data scientists to build products and solutions enabling the business to drive commercial growth and cost savings;
    Passionate hands on data scientist who wants an element of hands on delivery in their role. We need someone who can lead from the front, but equally someone who is happy to manage from a distance;
    Be an active member of the data community and represent the business as a leader across Data Science in both an internally and externally capacity;
    Passion for advanced and emerging technologies with an eagerness to implement them in a commercial capacity;
    Stakeholder management, the ability to explain data to non-data people and influence senior stakeholders is key to success;
    Demonstrated experience driving operational change through the use of data science and analytics;
    Strong technical skills across the data landscape.
   About You: With both permanent and contract positions available we encourage candidates with skills in the above area to contact the team at Hydrogen for confidential discussions. We are seeking intellectually capable,
    personable and change driven individuals who want to be part of a market leading consulting organisation. First class communication skills in both the written and verbal form will be required.What's on offer?          The opportunity to work with world class thought leaders in the digital transformation, Big data, Data science, RPA and AI space. International and local career progression. Competitive salaries depending on experience (role range from
    $200,000 + super - 300,000 + super and bonus).

  Role can be based in Melbourne or Sydney but travel will be required.
